 "title": "Countability of clopens in second countable profinite spaces",
 "statement": "Use the universes of [def-weil-size-convention]. Let $X$ be a compact Hausdorff totally disconnected topological space. The set of clopen subsets of $X$ (subsets that are both open and closed) is countable if and only if $X$ is second countable (has a countable basis of open subsets).",
